            <ArticleTitle>Antecedents of dental fear.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Early dental experiences were described in essay form by 225 college students reporting either &quot;high&quot; or &quot;low&quot; fear of dentistry. Antecedent factors which appeared to differentiate the two groups most clearly included pain experiences and dentist behaviors. Results were interpreted as supportive of a social-learning model of dental fear acquisition and their implications for dental training and practice were discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
